\description{
Surface state of the METRIC chain built from MODIS collection 6.1
products of tile h12v12 over the Cauquenes province (Maule Region,
Chile) for 15 February 2019 (UTC; Terra overpass), on the 1 km
sinusoidal grid of the MOD11A1 file. It is real data, not synthetic: the
layers are the output of the package's MODIS preprocessing applied to the
official granules listed under Source, with the options listed below.
Cells outside the province (official DPA 2023 boundary, cells touched by
the polygon) are \code{NA} in every layer, flag words included (not
evaluated).
}
\details{
The object is a packed \code{terra} raster (see \code{\link[terra:wrap]{terra::wrap()}}); use
\code{terra::unwrap(cauquenes_modis)} to get the \code{SpatRaster}.

Options of the assembly (explicit; none is a package default): LST of
MOD11A1 (Terra); white-sky shortwave albedo of MCD43A3 of the same day;
NDVI of the MOD13A2 composite whose period contains the date, matched per
pixel with its composite day; LAI of the MCD15A2H composite whose period
contains the date; 500 m inputs aggregated with the mean, only where
every 500 m sub-cell is valid; broadband emissivity from LAI (empirical
relation); LAI 0 assigned to the non-vegetated MCD15A2H classes 249-254
(flag \code{EF_SURF_LAI_ASSIGNED}, emissivity 0.95 there); QA policy \code{"flag"}
(QA findings are flagged, values are kept unless the product does not
provide them). Most of these choices are candidates pending
verification; the scene is meant for examples, tests and vignettes, not
for scientific results.

In the 3,779 cells of the province, LST is valid in 96.7 \% (the rest:
fill, clouds or not produced according to \code{QC_Day}), NDVI in 99.1 \% and
albedo, LAI and emissivity in practically all of them. Cells touched by
the coastline include sea (flag \code{EF_SURF_WATER} in NDVI and LAI).
}
